---
import CaseLayout from '../../layouts/CaseLayout.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/Figure.astro';
---

<CaseLayout
  headline="Designing a data product around an executive’s inquisitive moments."
  intro={[
    "After a large-scale migration of the internal dashboards I'd designed for the product, finance, marketing, sales, and executive teams, the Director of Data & Analytics asked me to explore how the same data could be made available to VP and C-level leaders on mobile devices.",
    'I set the brief, product requirements, interaction model, and mobile designs. The concept was presented to the C-suite and used to evaluate cost and feasibility.',
  ]}
  stakeholder="DocuSign"
  skills={['Speculative Design', 'Information Architecture', 'Interaction Design']}
  year="2023"
  role="Senior Product Designer"
  teamLabel="Team"
  teamMembers={[
    { name: 'Piyush Bhargava', role: 'Director, Product Management.' },
    { name: 'Arvind Toor', role: 'Sr. Director, Strategy and Business Operations.' },
  ]}
  hero="/assets/one-report/onereport-analysis-04.webp"
  heroWidth={3000}
  heroHeight={1688}
  heroViewportFit={false}
  theme="one-report"
  previousHref="/work/hbs-ai-institute/"
  nextHref="/work/global-data-analytics/"
>
  <section class="case-section reading-column" data-reveal>
    <h2>Deciding what to build.</h2>
    <p>Rather than approaching it as a mobile version of our existing dashboards, I approached it as an exploration to understand when, and for what reason, might an executive need to access data.</p>
    <div class="branched-layout">
      <p data-branch-lead><strong>Three exploratory scenarios shifted the focus from mobile dashboards to three purpose-built surfaces --</strong></p>
      <svg class="problem-connector" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path></path>
      </svg>
      <ol class="problem-list">
        <li><span class="problem-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>5-10 minute whitespaces during the day → Reports</span></li>
        <li><span class="problem-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Quick checks during meetings → Numbers</span></li>
        <li><span class="problem-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Exploratory deep dives when time allows → Analysis</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="media-grid three" data-reveal>
    <figure class="scenario-column" data-media-unit data-media-ready data-media-reveal-group>
      <div class="media-reveal-unit" data-media-reveal><div class="media-reveal-clip" data-media-reveal-clip><div class="media-reveal-rise" data-media-reveal-rise><button class="scenario-animation playable-media-surface" type="button" data-playable-media data-playback-mode="independent" aria-label="Pause 5-10 minute whitespace animation">
        <video src="/assets/one-report/video/sc-01.webm" poster="/assets/one-report/posters/sc-01.png" aria-label="5-10 minute whitespaces during the day" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" data-autoplay-on-view data-standalone-media></video>
      </button></div></div></div>
      <div class="media-reveal-unit" data-media-reveal><div class="media-reveal-clip" data-media-reveal-clip><div class="media-reveal-rise" data-media-reveal-rise><img src="/assets/one-report/sc-01.png" alt="Reports" width="1599" height="2955" loading="lazy" data-behance-image tabindex="0" role="button" data-container-media data-caption-anchor /></div></div></div>
      <figcaption data-media-caption>5-10 minute whitespaces during the day → Reports</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="scenario-column" data-media-unit data-media-ready data-media-reveal-group>
      <div class="media-reveal-unit" data-media-reveal><div class="media-reveal-clip" data-media-reveal-clip><div class="media-reveal-rise" data-media-reveal-rise><button class="scenario-animation playable-media-surface" type="button" data-playable-media data-playback-mode="independent" aria-label="Pause quick-check animation">
        <video src="/assets/one-report/video/sc-02.webm" poster="/assets/one-report/posters/sc-02.png" aria-label="Quick checks during meetings" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" data-autoplay-on-view data-standalone-media></video>
      </button></div></div></div>
      <div class="media-reveal-unit" data-media-reveal><div class="media-reveal-clip" data-media-reveal-clip><div class="media-reveal-rise" data-media-reveal-rise><img src="/assets/one-report/sc-02.png" alt="Numbers" width="1599" height="2955" loading="lazy" data-behance-image tabindex="0" role="button" data-container-media data-caption-anchor /></div></div></div>
      <figcaption data-media-caption>Quick checks during meetings → Numbers</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="scenario-column" data-media-unit data-media-ready data-media-reveal-group>
      <div class="media-reveal-unit" data-media-reveal><div class="media-reveal-clip" data-media-reveal-clip><div class="media-reveal-rise" data-media-reveal-rise><button class="scenario-animation playable-media-surface" type="button" data-playable-media data-playback-mode="independent" aria-label="Pause exploratory deep-dive animation">
        <video src="/assets/one-report/video/sc-03.webm" poster="/assets/one-report/posters/sc-03.png" aria-label="Exploratory deep dives when time allows" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" data-autoplay-on-view data-standalone-media></video>
      </button></div></div></div>
      <div class="media-reveal-unit" data-media-reveal><div class="media-reveal-clip" data-media-reveal-clip><div class="media-reveal-rise" data-media-reveal-rise><img src="/assets/one-report/sc-03.png" alt="Analysis" width="1599" height="2955" loading="lazy" data-behance-image tabindex="0" role="button" data-container-media data-caption-anchor /></div></div></div>
      <figcaption data-media-caption>Exploratory deep dives when time allows → Analysis</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <section class="case-section reading-column" data-reveal>
    <h2>Designing ‘Analysis’</h2>
    <p>Reviewing dashboards across departments showed that the same business unit could be a metric, dimension, or filter depending on the team. I needed one analytical layer that supported all three roles.</p>
    <p>To create a single analytical layer that supported all three roles, I designed Analysis as a Sankey flow, letting users trace a metric through Partners, Region, Product, Channel, and Customers.</p>
    <p>Focus and Filters drew from the same dataset and its subsets.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="media-stack one-report-scenarios" data-reveal>
    <Figure
      src="/assets/one-report/onereport-analysis-01.webp"
      alt="Churn Flow with swappable columns"
      caption="Swapping a column redraws the same report through a different dimension. Here, Churn Flow shifts from Channel to Product, keeping the same surface usable to understand product/revenue and sales/distribution."
      width={3000}
      height={1688}
      viewportFit={false}
    />
    <Figure
      src="/assets/one-report/onereport-analysis-02.webp"
      alt="Analysis flow connected to reports and numbers"
      caption="Tracing a single metric across the Analysis layer, showing how it connects to Reports and Numbers views."
      width={3000}
      height={1688}
      viewportFit={false}
    />
    <Figure
      src="/assets/one-report/onereport-analysis-03.webp"
      alt="Focus and Filters on the same dataset"
      caption="Focus and Filters operating on the same dataset — Focus narrows the scope, Filters refine within it."
      width={3000}
      height={1688}
      viewportFit={false}
    />
  </div>

  <section class="case-section reading-column" data-reveal>
    <h2>Designing ‘Reports’</h2>
    <p>Internal reports were already dense on desktop, so moving them to mobile required a clearer hierarchy.</p>
    <p>I designed Reports as a fixed, card-based layout inspired by elements of a digital news report, using sheets to reveal detail progressively and visuals to clarify dense datasets. This preserved access to every metric without overwhelming executives.</p>
  </section>

  <Figure
    src="/assets/one-report/onereport-report.webp"
    alt="Report layout with progressively revealed chart detail"
    caption="Report layout inspired by elements of a digital news report, with sheets revealing chart detail."
    width={3000}
    height={1688}
    viewportFit={false}
  />

  <section class="case-section reading-column" data-reveal>
    <h2>Designing ‘Numbers’</h2>
    <p>This surface centered on a user finding a metric during a call, making time-to-value critical.</p>
    <p>I used a search bar rather than a chat box to signal that short phrases were enough—a behavior validated in prototype testing with directors. Although the interface suggested sophisticated AI, the result could be delivered without LLMs using lower-cost NLP frameworks. That path enabled the project to move into cost estimation.</p>
  </section>

  <Figure
    src="/assets/one-report/onereport-insights.webp"
    alt="Search-based data visualization interface"
    caption="The interface infering the right visualization from the phrasing alone, escalating from a number to a comparison to a trend."
    width={3000}
    height={1688}
    viewportFit={false}
  />

  <section class="case-section reading-column" data-reveal>
    <h2>Outcome and Takeaway:</h2>
    <p>The application was tested with five chiefs of staff who acted as proxies for the C-suite and was later demoed to DocuSign's C-suite directly.</p>
    <p>It then went through a cost estimation cycle and was subsequently shelved alongside several other company-wide initiatives as part of budget cuts following DocuSign's decision to acquire of Lexicon.</p>
    <p>Despite being a speculative initiative, <strong>the application resonated with executives because it was designed around moments in the life cycle of an executive</strong> rather than as a mobile version of existing reporting infrastructure.</p>
  </section>
</CaseLayout>
